{
  "_readme": "Persona registry. pool: which assignment slots a persona can fill (expert = matched to the exact subfield, adjacent = neighbouring CV area, outsider = keyword mismatch). reading_view: front|skim|main|full (see hxlib/panel.py VIEW_SECTIONS). reads_supplement: no|if_needed|yes. draw_weight: relative frequency of the matching primary reviewer type in 184 real CV reviews (01_sources/real_review_patterns.md sec. 5: expert-constructive 27% -> R03/R05/R13, terse 18% -> R09/R16, novelty skeptic 12.5%, benchmark-table 10%, checklist 9% -> R10/R07, champion 8%, theory 6.5%, LLM-generic 5-14% -> R15, practitioner 2%, hostile 0.5%; R08/R14 not separately coded, set low). Axes follow AgentReview (commitment, intention, knowledgeability). leniency: fixed rating offset in scale levels vs a calibrated reviewer (close experts harsher, out-of-domain and LLM-assisted milder; 01_sources/reviewer_behavior_literature.md rules 2, 4, 14). killer: adversarial persona; draw panels hold at most one (rule 3). New I/M/N personas are curated venue-guided lenses, not measured reviewer frequencies; their draw weights are not empirical. role: reviewer (drawn into panels) or figure_reviewer (F01, the harness instrument behind the opt-in `hx.py new --figures` job; never drawn, available to every venue).",
